# User-unit presets for the Lisa image.
#
# systemd's DEFAULT preset policy for user units is "enable", so any
# package that ships a user service quietly starts it for every user —
# the dependency-installed-surfaces trap (#161's podman.socket, and now
# fluidsynth). fluidsynth arrives as a codec dependency, its user
# service opens the CS8409 PCM raw at login, and whichever of it and
# WirePlumber loses the device race leaves the desktop on Dummy
# Output — speakers dead with everything "active". A synth nobody
# asked for must not own the sound card.
disable fluidsynth.service

# NO catch-all here, deliberately (#336). Presets are first-match-wins
# in lexicographic FILE order, so an `enable *` in a 00- file preempts
# every later 01-lisa-*.preset — the first preset-all would have
# re-enabled the podman REST socket that #130/#161 closed. Units no
# file mentions fall through to systemd's own default, which for user
# units is enable; anything that must stay off gets its own explicit
# line, here or in a later file.
